This was my first ascension on NAO. Even though I've ascended about ten
times locally, for some reason it feels different to have people
peering virtually over your shoulder. I was randomly assigned a chaotic
female orcish barbarian. Despite a number of stupid mistakes, enough
reminders to "take your hands off the keyboard and think" sank in to
allow a pretty easy ascension.

Extremely helpful scroll shop on DL2. Spent a couple thousand turns
price-IDing scrolls; I had food to spare. By T:3700, blessed IDed
everything for sure. Nearly bit it through sheer stupidity at least
twice (a fox and a goblin).

Mine entrance on DL4, decided to move on to Sokoban, on DL7. By T:9000
(pretty slow), got the BoH. Nearly bit it on the way to Soko to a
kobold shaman.

Entered the mines at T:10000. Minetown at T:11000 yielded a magic
marker, magic whistle, and enough candles for the eventual invocation.
Extended thievery and slaughter of the guard. Nearly bit it to a gnome
lord and some grey elves. Lost dog to the watch captain. Still no key,
credit card, or lock pick.

Continued back in the dungeon for intrinsics and adventure. Extended
bout on DL12 with a cursed elven dagger stuck to my hand (stupid);
should have retreated earlier for the remove curse. Spent a couple of
?EA to get the AC down to -4.

Quest portal showed up on DL13. Consecutive shops on DL12,DL13,DL14.
Still no MR/reflection, so it's time to dive for the Castle at T:15250,
XL10, AC-4.

Good luck, found an unguarded altar on DL15. Converted it, blessed up
some water, and brought down the stash.

T:16750 was nearly the end of the game again. I was playing late at
night without much sleep, hoping to sacrifest for the Cleaver. Then, I
got hit by a black light (no unihorn yet).  Bad move #1 was not waiting
out the hallucinations; instead, I killed and sacrified a hobgoblin
(coracial) while trying to kill several other creatures I knew were
chickatrices. Enter Juiblex--I'm still hallucinating, and in bad move
#2 I accidentally take on the slimy demon prince at XL10. As I'm
engulfed, thought #1 is, "Great, here goes another character." Thought
#2 is, "I at least have to kill Jubi, or else this could end up being
one of those bones file traps." So I smite away with the +2 axe, and
green & is dead (looked like an owlbear to me...) in a few turns. XL11,
for what it's worth, and the hallucinations go away. So now I'm Ill,
with no unihorn, and have maybe half a dozen turns to figure out how to
fix the problem. Step 1, #pray: Set is displeased (probably for my
previous bad moves). At least the adjacent chickatrice didn't stone me.
Step 2, check the inventory for anything. Yup, there in the comestibles
is an eucalyptus leaf! What a relief! Despite a few more futile
sacrifices and another near-death experience with a rock troll, I press
on and get Cleaver at T:17826.

Still no MR/reflection, so continue down with caution towards the
castle. On the way down, a helpful guard barracks provides the
requisite bugle. No titan, and Medusa dies on DL26 around T:20250. Dig
down a couple levels to the castle at DL28. Decided not to use the
drawbridge tactic to save wands, which probably was a waste of time
since the soldiers expended many of the charges anyway. Got the wishing
wand and brought it back to the stash, IDed as 0:2. Fortunately, I had
already IDed a scroll of charging, so no need to wish any up. First
wish is for bfg +2 SDSM, then bfg +2 CoMR. Recharge the wand, bf +2
boots of jumping, bf +2 GoP, bf +2 helm of telepathy. With AC-13, MR,
reflection, and one more wrestable wish, time to go find Ludios.

T:23647 Found the portal on DL20. For spite, there's a silver dragon
that drops scales. Nothing useful from the throne, 45k gold for the
trouble. Back to Minetown to get some protection, a total of 9 points.
For kicks, I go and clear out the lower half of the mines, and lucky me
finds another magic marker. I did go and kill the watch captain to pay
him back for my dog.

T:28675 Trip back to the castle to explore the back half. Nearly die to
a yellow dragon before remembering to Elbereth. The treasure rooms turn
out to be completely useless, but I'm XL14 and it's time for the quest.
Thoth Amon dies miserably, and it's back to the stash for some
enchanting. By T:31150, AC is -35 and I'm ready for Gehennom.

T:32850 and the Valley of the Dead is boring. Next level down is
Asmodeus, who I bribe and move past. DL32 is Jubi's lair, but he's been
dead for nigh on 15000 turns now :)

DL34 holds the first purple L, but I'm well-prepared with E-ngraving
tools, and he dies fast. Another purple L at Baalzebub's lair on DL36
meets the same fate. Baal is as easily bribed as his predecessor, and
I'm moving on. The Wizard shows up on radar at DL39. Another purple L
at DL41, the geno-trigger-finger is getting close, but they're just an
annoyance so I keep the conduct.

As I get to DL42, I realize I haven't found Vlad's place yet; I
backtrack and find the entrance on DL40. I'm really only here for three
things (AoLS, BoWW, and the candlabrum) but a few useful potions turn
up anyhow, and I find the first blue dragon for shock resistance.

Orcustown is DL43. Not much of use, but a blessed ID nets me several
handy rings including free action and teleport control. Orcus himself
turns out to be a major pain in the butt, since in trying to save the
wand of death I let him get away a couple of times, and he
spam-summoned a bunch of creatures that got in the way of capturing the
wand.

Found the portal to Rodney's tower and went to clean it out. Conflict
and a purple worm on the second level made for some amusement. Moved on
down and marked the VS on DL51 around T:45000, then worked backwards
while digging paths... an endeavor that took until T:49700. Fortunately
there were several levels where the stairs were close to each other.

Back at the stash, enchanted and fireproofed the WW boots for a final
AC of -39. One more trip to Minetown to get those candles, then batch
up some holy water, alchemize for HP, and... decide that I don't want
to try and ascend with a two handed weapon. Sacrifest to get a Brand
(it was Frost) at T:53243, enchanted it and a silver saber up to +7/+6,
and learned two-weapon fighting. Write up a few scrolls of gold
detection, and it's off to see the Wizard...

Blasted the Wizard with digging and death at T:55828, c?tele down, and
performed the invocation. c?tele into the sanctum and readied conflict.
The door was on the 4th side I checked, and the high priest had a cloak
of magic resistance--I wasted 3 death charges on him, too. c!oGL out
and begin the run up. For some reason there's more adrenaline when you
know people are watching. Mysterious force at DL36, DL34 (three times),
and DL33 (twice). Just when I thought I was safe, the Wizard showed up
on DL30; he fell quickly to ice and silver. I reached the castle
T:56800. After passing it by, I realized I hadn't bothered to stock up
on food; fortunately I had a =oSD.

Malignant aura cursed my silver saber at DL20, causing a brief detour
to find where I had dropped it. I took the time to recharge the wand of
death. Rodney reappeared on DL16 and just as quickly disappeared.
Stopped briefly at the stash, _again_ forgetting to grab food. On to
the final test with no more excitement.

On Earth, I realized my next failing... I had plenty of gold detection
but not enough confusion. The one spell I had learned was too recent to
be of value. I found a magic lamp, of all random things, just before
portalling to Air. A random Archon could have been trouble, but I flew
past him and on to Fire. There I hoped to get by without using up my
last !oBooze; instead, I wasted a lot of time circling the level and
ended up having to race an Archon to the portal instead. On Water, I
cursed all my remaining scrolls of gold detection, ran to the right
side of the plane and hoped for the best. I had great luck in locating
the portal with the first scroll, and needed only one more to home in.

On Astral, Famine was one the left and so was I, so I went there first.
One final purple L made an appearance, but I smote him and switched
over to the jumping boots. I jumped a large circle around Famine, but
she caught up to me just at the middle door; a blast from the death
wand solved that problem. Teleporting my adversaries aside, I jumped
into the high temple and discovered it was my own. Leaving my guardian
angel
behind...

